NVIDIA primary scanout retirement workaround for wlroots 0.20.2.
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Local C adaptation prepared with Codex for notdevblue, 2026-11-07.

Adaptation of the lifetime strategy discussed in Smithay PR 2151 and Jay
PR 1317, not a verbatim upstream backport; both remain open as of 2026-11-07.
https://github.com/Smithay/smithay/pull/2151
Strategy reference: Smithay 0c649d2d6824b60b7bfe27f1fdb5f2fbf4311ac4.
https://github.com/mahkoh/jay/pull/1317
Strategy reference: Jay a5799f78064c5777e52c99cb995d2d0dc412ce63.
https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/387955

Keep the preceding primary FB and its release timeline until the following
synchronous flip. Force composition and software cursors on nvidia-drm to
avoid holding both buffers of a double-buffered direct-scanout client.
This changes neither color format nor HDR metadata and adds no queued frame.
Costs one extra compositor buffer and loses direct-scanout/hardware-cursor
optimizations. Optional libliftoff layers fall back to composition; tearing
commits are rejected because retirement needs synchronous page-flip spacing.
WLR_DRM_NVIDIA_DELAYED_RELEASE=0 disables the local workaround.
Driver fix is still required; physical-panel A/B validation remains required.

